IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part XV, ss 187 and 188: CONTINUANCE.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. "Continuance" moves a corporation from one statute to another without winding it
-- up. Section 187 brings a body corporate from elsewhere INTO this Act ("import"); section 188 takes a
-- corporation OUT of this Act, to another jurisdiction or under one of the other federal Acts
-- ("export"). The Director's duties are encoded for what they mean to the corporation: the duty arises
-- on receipt, and the effect on the date shown in the certificate.
--
-- Subsection 188(2.1) is repealed in this text; subsection 188(7) still points at "the Acts referred to
-- in subsection (2.1)". That list is in subsection (2), and I read the reference as pointing there
-- (fork F3, in the register).

§§ `s 187 Continuance (import)`

-- src:2275 | 187 (1) A body corporate incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament may, if so authorized by the laws of the jurisdiction where it is incorporated, apply to the Director for a certificate of continuance.
@ref CBCA s 187(1) (src:2275)
GIVEN `the body corporate was incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws of the jurisdiction where it is incorporated authorize it to apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the body corporate may apply to the Director for a certificate of continuance within s 187(1)` MEANS
        `the body corporate was incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament`
    AND `the laws of the jurisdiction where it is incorporated authorize it to apply`

-- The amendment may be made by the articles of continuance "without so stating": nothing more is
-- required of the applicant beyond the amendment being one the Act lets a corporation make.
-- src:2276 | Amendments in articles of continuance
-- src:2277 | (2) A body corporate that applies for continuance under subsection (1) may, without so stating in its articles of continuance, effect by those articles any amendment to its Act of incorporation, articles, letters patent or memorandum or articles of association if the amendment is an amendment a corporation incorporated under this Act may make to its articles.
@ref CBCA s 187(2) (src:2277)
GIVEN `the body corporate applies for continuance under subsection 187(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment is one a corporation incorporated under this Act may make to its articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles of continuance may effect the amendment without stating it within s 187(2)` MEANS
        `the body corporate applies for continuance under subsection 187(1)`
    AND `the amendment is one a corporation incorporated under this Act may make to its articles`

-- src:2278 | Articles of continuance
-- src:2279 | (3) Articles of continuance in the form that the Director fixes shall be sent to the Director together with the documents required by sections 19 and 106.
@ref CBCA s 187(3) (src:2279)
GIVEN `the articles of continuance are in the form the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: sections 19 and 106 (pieces cb1 and cb2)
      `the documents required by sections 19 and 106 are sent with them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles of continuance have been sent as s 187(3) requires` MEANS
        `the articles of continuance are in the form the Director fixes`
    AND `the documents required by sections 19 and 106 are sent with them`

-- src:2280 | Certificate of continuance
-- src:2281 | (4) On receipt of articles of continuance, the Director shall issue a certificate of continuance in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 187(4) (src:2281)
GIVEN `the Director has received articles of continuance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of continuance within s 187(4)` MEANS
    `the Director has received articles of continuance`

-- The effects begin "on the date shown in the certificate of continuance".
-- src:2282 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2283 | (5) On the date shown in the certificate of continuance
@ref CBCA s 187(5), helper (src:2283)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day is on or after the date shown in the certificate of continuance` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the date shown in the certificate of continuance`

-- src:2284 | (a) the body corporate becomes a corporation to which this Act applies as if it had been incorporated under this Act;
@ref CBCA s 187(5)(a) (src:2284)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the body corporate is a corporation to which this Act applies on a day within s 187(5)(a)` MEANS
    `the day is on or after the date shown in the certificate of continuance` `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` `the day asked about`

-- src:2285 | (b) the articles of continuance are deemed to be the articles of incorporation of the continued corporation; and
@ref CBCA s 187(5)(b) (src:2285)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles of continuance are deemed the articles of incorporation on a day within s 187(5)(b)` MEANS
    `the day is on or after the date shown in the certificate of continuance` `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` `the day asked about`

-- src:2286 | (c) the certificate of continuance is deemed to be the certificate of incorporation of the continued corporation.
@ref CBCA s 187(5)(c) (src:2286)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the certificate of continuance is deemed the certificate of incorporation on a day within s 187(5)(c)` MEANS
    `the day is on or after the date shown in the certificate of continuance` `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` `the day asked about`

-- "Forthwith" is a word the Act does not turn into a number of days. The duty is encoded as arising on
-- the issue of the certificate; no deadline is invented.
-- src:2287 | Copy of certificate
-- src:2288 | (6) The Director shall forthwith send a copy of the certificate of continuance to the appropriate official or public body in the jurisdiction in which continuance under this Act was authorized.
@ref CBCA s 187(6) (src:2288)
GIVEN `the Director has issued a certificate of continuance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must send a copy of the certificate to the official or body of the home jurisdiction within s 187(6)` MEANS
    `the Director has issued a certificate of continuance`

-- "When a body corporate is continued as a corporation under this Act" -- each paragraph then holds.
-- src:2289 | Rights preserved
-- src:2290 | (7) When a body corporate is continued as a corporation under this Act,
-- src:2291 | (a) the property of the body corporate continues to be the property of the corporation;
@ref CBCA s 187(7)(a) (src:2291)
GIVEN `the body corporate has been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the property of the body corporate continues to be the corporation's within s 187(7)(a)` MEANS
    `the body corporate has been continued as a corporation under this Act`

-- src:2292 | (b) the corporation continues to be liable for the obligations of the body corporate;
@ref CBCA s 187(7)(b) (src:2292)
GIVEN `the body corporate has been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation continues to be liable for the body corporate's obligations within s 187(7)(b)` MEANS
    `the body corporate has been continued as a corporation under this Act`

-- src:2293 | (c) an existing cause of action, claim or liability to prosecution is unaffected;
@ref CBCA s 187(7)(c) (src:2293)
GIVEN `the body corporate has been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an existing cause of action, claim or liability to prosecution is unaffected by the continuance within s 187(7)(c)` MEANS
    `the body corporate has been continued as a corporation under this Act`

-- src:2294 | (d) a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding pending by or against the body corporate may be continued to be prosecuted by or against the corporation; and
@ref CBCA s 187(7)(d) (src:2294)
GIVEN `the body corporate has been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a pending proceeding by or against the body corporate may be continued by or against the corporation within s 187(7)(d)` MEANS
    `the body corporate has been continued as a corporation under this Act`

-- src:2295 | (e) a conviction against, or ruling, order or judgment in favour of or against, the body corporate may be enforced by or against the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 187(7)(e) (src:2295)
GIVEN `the body corporate has been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a conviction, ruling, order or judgment may be enforced by or against the corporation within s 187(7)(e)` MEANS
    `the body corporate has been continued as a corporation under this Act`

-- (8): "subject to subsections (9) and 49(8)". Section 49(8) (piece cb2) is a plain input: where it
-- applies to the share, the deeming does not. The second sentence preserves the holder's rights and
-- liabilities; both sentences speak only of a share issued BEFORE the continuance, so for any other share
-- the subsection says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:2296 | Issued shares
-- src:2297 | (8) Subject to subsections (9) and 49(8), a share of a body corporate issued before the body corporate was continued under this Act is deemed to have been issued in compliance with this Act and with the provisions of the articles of continuance irrespective of whether the share is fully paid and irrespective of any designation, rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions set out on or referred to in the certificate representing the share. Continuance under this section does not deprive a holder of any right or privilege that the holder claims under, or relieve the holder of any liability in respect of, an issued share.
@ref CBCA s 187(8) (src:2297)
GIVEN `the share was issued before the body corporate was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 49(8) (piece cb2)
      `section 49(8) applies to the share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the share is deemed to have been issued in compliance with this Act within s 187(8)` MEANS
    IF `the share was issued before the body corporate was continued under this Act`
    THEN JUST (NOT `section 49(8) applies to the share`)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref CBCA s 187(8) (src:2297)
GIVEN `the share was issued before the body corporate was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the holder keeps the rights and the liabilities in respect of the share within s 187(8)` MEANS
    IF `the share was issued before the body corporate was continued under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (9): the prohibition. It applies when the holder of a registered certificate convertible to bearer form
-- exercises the conversion privilege.
-- src:2298 | Convertible shares
-- src:2299 | (9) If a corporation continued under this Act had, before it was so continued, issued a share certificate in registered form that is convertible to bearer form, the corporation shall not, if a holder of such a share certificate exercises the conversion privilege attached to the certificate, issue a share certificate in bearer form.
@ref CBCA s 187(9) (src:2299)
GIVEN `the share certificate was issued in registered form before continuance and is convertible to bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder exercises the conversion privilege` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may issue a share certificate in bearer form within s 187(9)` MEANS
    NOT (    `the share certificate was issued in registered form before continuance and is convertible to bearer form`
         AND `the holder exercises the conversion privilege`)

-- (10): "share includes" the three kinds of instrument. A closed list: another kind of instrument is
-- not a share unless it is "a like instrument", which is a judgment (an input).
-- src:2300 | Definition of share
-- src:2301 | (10) For the purposes of subsections (8) and (9), share includes an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1), a share warrant as defined in the Canada Corporations Act, chapter C-32 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, or a like instrument.
@ref CBCA s 187(10) (src:2301)
DECLARE `Kind of instrument for s 187(10)` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary share`
    `an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1)`
    `a share warrant as defined in the Canada Corporations Act`
    `a like instrument`
    `an instrument that is none of these`

@ref CBCA s 187(10) (src:2301)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of instrument for s 187(10)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instrument is a share for subsections 187(8) and 187(9) within s 187(10)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an ordinary share` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a share warrant as defined in the Canada Corporations Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a like instrument` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (11), (12): par value shares.
-- src:2302 | Where continued reference to par value shares permissible
-- src:2303 | (11) Where the Director determines, on the application of a body corporate, that it is not practicable to change a reference to the nominal or par value of shares of a class or series that the body corporate was authorized to issue before it was continued under this Act, the Director may, notwithstanding subsection 24(1), permit the body corporate to continue to refer in its articles to those shares, whether issued or unissued, as shares having a nominal or par value.
@ref CBCA s 187(11) (src:2303)
GIVEN `the body corporate applied to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director determines that it is not practicable to change the reference to nominal or par value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may permit continued reference to par value shares within s 187(11)` MEANS
        `the body corporate applied to the Director`
    AND `the Director determines that it is not practicable to change the reference to nominal or par value`

-- src:2304 | Limitation
-- src:2305 | (12) A corporation shall set out in its articles the maximum number of shares of a class or series referred to in subsection (11) and may not amend its articles to increase that maximum number of shares or to change the nominal or par value of those shares.
@ref CBCA s 187(12) (src:2305)
GIVEN `the corporation has been permitted to continue to refer to par value shares under subsection 187(11)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles set out the maximum number of shares of the class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles comply with the duty to set out the maximum number within s 187(12)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation has been permitted to continue to refer to par value shares under subsection 187(11)`)
    OR  `the articles set out the maximum number of shares of the class or series`

@ref CBCA s 187(12) (src:2305)
GIVEN `the corporation has been permitted to continue to refer to par value shares under subsection 187(11)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment increases the maximum number of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment changes the nominal or par value of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may make the amendment within s 187(12)` MEANS
    NOT (    `the corporation has been permitted to continue to refer to par value shares under subsection 187(11)`
         AND (    `the amendment increases the maximum number of those shares`
              OR  `the amendment changes the nominal or par value of those shares`))

§§ `s 188 Continuance (export)`

-- (10) is the condition the other jurisdiction's laws must meet; (1) is "subject to" it. All five limbs.
-- src:2327 | Prohibition
-- src:2328 | (10) A corporation shall not be continued as a body corporate under the laws of another jurisdiction unless those laws provide in effect that
-- src:2329 | (a) the property of the corporation continues to be the property of the body corporate;
-- src:2330 | (b) the body corporate continues to be liable for the obligations of the corporation;
-- src:2331 | (c) an existing cause of action, claim or liability to prosecution is unaffected;
-- src:2332 | (d) a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding pending by or against the corporation may be continued to be prosecuted by or against the body corporate; and
-- src:2333 | (e) a conviction against, or ruling, order or judgment in favour of or against, the corporation may be enforced by or against the body corporate.
@ref CBCA s 188(10) (src:2328-2333)
GIVEN `the laws provide that the property of the corporation continues to be the property of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws provide that the body corporate continues to be liable for the corporation's obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws provide that an existing cause of action, claim or liability to prosecution is unaffected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws provide that a pending proceeding by or against the corporation may be continued by or against the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws provide that a conviction, ruling, order or judgment may be enforced by or against the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may be continued under the laws of another jurisdiction within s 188(10)` MEANS
        `the laws provide that the property of the corporation continues to be the property of the body corporate`
    AND `the laws provide that the body corporate continues to be liable for the corporation's obligations`
    AND `the laws provide that an existing cause of action, claim or liability to prosecution is unaffected`
    AND `the laws provide that a pending proceeding by or against the corporation may be continued by or against the body corporate`
    AND `the laws provide that a conviction, ruling, order or judgment may be enforced by or against the body corporate`

-- src:2306 | Continuance — other jurisdictions
-- src:2307 | 188 (1) Subject to subsection (10), a corporation may apply to the appropriate official or public body of another jurisdiction requesting that the corporation be continued as if it had been incorporated under the laws of that other jurisdiction if the corporation
-- src:2308 | (a) is authorized by the shareholders in accordance with this section to make the application; and
-- src:2309 | (b) establishes to the satisfaction of the Director that its proposed continuance in the other jurisdiction will not adversely affect creditors or shareholders of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 188(1) (src:2307-2309)
GIVEN `the shareholders authorized the application in accordance with section 188` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation establishes to the satisfaction of the Director that the proposed continuance will not adversely affect creditors or shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws of the other jurisdiction satisfy subsection 188(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may apply to another jurisdiction to be continued within s 188(1)` MEANS
        `the shareholders authorized the application in accordance with section 188`
    AND `the corporation establishes to the satisfaction of the Director that the proposed continuance will not adversely affect creditors or shareholders`
    AND `the laws of the other jurisdiction satisfy subsection 188(10)`

-- (2): to the appropriate Minister, under the Bank Act, the Canada Cooperatives Act, the Cooperative
-- Credit Associations Act, the Insurance Companies Act or the Trust and Loan Companies Act.
-- src:2310 | Continuance — other federal Acts
-- src:2311 | (2) A corporation that is authorized by the shareholders in accordance with this section may apply to the appropriate Minister for its continuance under the Bank Act, the Canada Cooperatives Act, the Cooperative Credit Associations Act, the Insurance Companies Act or the Trust and Loan Companies Act.
-- src:2312 | (2.1) [Repealed, 2001, c. 14, s. 92]
@ref CBCA s 188(2) (src:2311)
GIVEN `the shareholders authorized the application in accordance with section 188` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is for continuance under one of the listed federal Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may apply to the appropriate Minister for continuance under another federal Act within s 188(2)` MEANS
        `the shareholders authorized the application in accordance with section 188`
    AND `the application is for continuance under one of the listed federal Acts`

-- src:2313 | Notice of meeting
-- src:2314 | (3) A notice of a meeting of shareholders complying with section 135 shall be sent in accordance with that section to each shareholder and shall state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190, but failure to make that statement does not invalidate a discontinuance under this Act.
@ref CBCA s 188(3) (src:2314)
GIVEN -- out of range: section 135 (piece cb3)
      `the notice complies with section 135` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is sent to each shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice of the meeting complies within s 188(3)` MEANS
        `the notice complies with section 135`
    AND `the notice is sent to each shareholder`
    AND (    (NOT `a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190`)
         OR  `the notice states that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares`)

@ref CBCA s 188(3) (src:2314)
GIVEN `the omission of the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Effect on validity of leaving out the dissent statement`
`the effect on the discontinuance of leaving out the dissent statement within s 188(3)` MEANS
    `the effect of leaving out the dissent statement` `the omission of the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice`

-- src:2315 | Right to vote
-- src:2316 | (4) Each share of the corporation carries the right to vote in respect of a continuance whether or not it otherwise carries the right to vote.
@ref CBCA s 188(4) (src:2316)
GIVEN `the share otherwise carries the right to vote` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the share carries the right to vote on the continuance within s 188(4)` MEANS TRUE

-- src:2317 | Shareholder approval
-- src:2318 | (5) An application for continuance becomes authorized when the shareholders voting thereon have approved of the continuance by a special resolution.
@ref CBCA s 188(5) (src:2318)
GIVEN tally IS A `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application for continuance is authorized within s 188(5)` MEANS
    `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally

-- src:2319 | Termination
-- src:2320 | (6) The directors of a corporation may, if authorized by the shareholders at the time of approving an application for continuance under this section, abandon the application without further approval of the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 188(6) (src:2320)
GIVEN `the shareholders authorized the directors to abandon the application when they approved it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may abandon the application without further approval of the shareholders within s 188(6)` MEANS
    `the shareholders authorized the directors to abandon the application when they approved it`

-- (7). Subsection (2.1) is repealed; "the Acts referred to in subsection (2.1)" is read as the Acts listed
-- in subsection (2) (fork F3). A "notice satisfactory to the Director" is a plain input.
-- src:2321 | Discontinuance
-- src:2322 | (7) On receipt of a notice satisfactory to the Director that the corporation has been continued under the laws of another jurisdiction or under one of the Acts referred to in subsection (2.1), the Director shall file the notice and issue a certificate of discontinuance in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 188(7) (src:2322)
GIVEN `the Director has received a notice that the corporation has been continued under the laws of another jurisdiction or under one of the listed federal Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is satisfactory to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must file the notice and issue a certificate of discontinuance within s 188(7)` MEANS
        `the Director has received a notice that the corporation has been continued under the laws of another jurisdiction or under one of the listed federal Acts`
    AND `the notice is satisfactory to the Director`

-- src:2323 | Notice deemed to be articles
-- src:2324 | (8) For the purposes of section 262, a notice referred to in subsection (7) is deemed to be articles that are in the form that the Director fixes.
@ref CBCA s 188(8) (src:2324)
GIVEN `the document is a notice referred to in subsection 188(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice is deemed to be articles in the form the Director fixes for section 262 within s 188(8)` MEANS
    `the document is a notice referred to in subsection 188(7)`

-- (9): the Act ceases to apply on the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance (fork F2: it applies
-- strictly before that date).
-- src:2325 | Rights preserved
-- src:2326 | (9) This Act ceases to apply to the corporation on the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance.
@ref CBCA s 188(9) (src:2326)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Act still applies to the corporation on a day within s 188(9)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance`
